<!-- brute force  -->

	    Here its a heapify function that basically convert tree (unordered data) into heap 
	    
	    and we know in any heap like min/max heap the 
	    first element of array or the root of the tree is the min/max element respectively
	    
	    let's consider max heap scenario in which we need to make sort ascending
	    so what we do basically first convert unordered data into heap (tc n sc logn)
	    now first element of array is max of all 
	    so we do swap with the last index 
	    
	    then again we convert all data into heap excluding the last index 
	    then again swap ... and so on
	    
	    tc- n2
	    sc- logn







<!-- optimal -->

first of all do build heap (do max heap in ascending )
	   
	   then we know that top element of the heap is the largest 
	   swap it to last index 
	   
	   now basically the current top index value in that heap is not 
	   in its correct position other element are unchanged so its 
	   basically in its right place 
	   
	   so do heapify for top element only which is single element by excluding the last index because its in its right place
	   
	   now we again have max heap created so swap with second last 
	   index 
	   
	   and continue this process until you got sorted array 
	   
	   Tc (buildHeap) n + (loop over array * single heapify call) nlogn ~ nlogn
	   Sc - build heap (logn) + single heapify call logn ~ logn